THE OPS WEEKLY - Issue #212

This week: why peak staffing plans written in June are already late, a teardown of three AMR deployments that missed their ROI targets, and the five metrics every DC manager should stop reporting.

1. Peak staffing is a Q2 problem
Temp agencies in the Mountain West report that 40% of Q4 seasonal capacity is already committed.

2. AMR ROI teardowns
The common thread: robots were added without changing how work was released to the floor.

3. Stop reporting these five metrics
Lines per hour without order mix is noise.

